-- Q10980: Individual Taxation: Deductions [medium/L2]
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Take the standard deduction because the age 65+ addition brings his total to about $16,950","Itemize because his $15,800 in expenses exceeds the $15,000 base standard deduction","Take the standard deduction because taxpayers over age 65 are prohibited from itemizing","Itemize because the additional standard deduction applies only to married joint filers"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under IRC Section 63(f), taxpayers age 65 or older receive an additional standard deduction (~$1,950 for single filers in 2026), bringing Mitchell''s total to approximately $16,950. Since this exceeds his $15,800 in itemizable expenses, the standard deduction is more beneficial.
Wrong (B): Comparing $15,800 only to the $15,000 base ignores the additional standard deduction for age 65+, which raises the total above Mitchell''s itemizable expenses.
Wrong (C): Being over 65 does not prohibit itemizing; the additional amount simply makes the standard deduction more competitive for many older taxpayers.
