-- Q11048: Individual Taxation: Income [hard/L4]
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["$0 deductible because the entire $18,000 is suspended at the passive activity tier","$18,000 fully deductible against Crawford''s $50,000 in wage income","$18,000 passes basis and at-risk but is fully suspended as a passive activity loss","$12,000 deductible with the remaining $6,000 suspended at the at-risk tier"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under the three-tier loss limitation framework, losses pass sequentially through basis (Section 704(d)), at-risk (Section 465), then passive activity (Section 469). Crawford''s $18,000 loss clears the $30,000 basis limit and $22,000 at-risk amount but is fully suspended under Section 469 because he has no passive income to offset.
Wrong (A): While the result is $0 currently deductible, this answer incorrectly implies the loss is initially stopped at the passive tier without passing through basis and at-risk first.
Wrong (B): Crawford does not materially participate, so the loss cannot be deducted against wages under Section 469 passive activity rules.
Wrong (D): Crawford''s at-risk amount of $22,000 exceeds the $18,000 loss, so nothing is suspended at the at-risk tier.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 11048;

