-- Q11117: Partnerships [medium/L2]
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["$70,000, equal to the built-in gain that existed at the time of contribution","$90,000, representing the total current gain over Abbott''s original $40,000 basis","$0, because the property is distributed back to the original contributing partner","$20,000, representing only the post-contribution appreciation in property value"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under Section 704(c)(1)(B), if contributed property with built-in gain is distributed to another partner within 7 years, the contributing partner must recognize the built-in gain. However, when the property is distributed back to the original contributing partner, this rule does not apply and no gain is triggered.
